reated 75 minutes after Pending Close and is recorded POSTED. On those reported event facts and the directly read Oracle policy, POSTED is inconsistent with the documented treatment for a newly created non-exception transaction. This is a peer-supported finding, not a claim of independent access to this job's event source.\\\",\\n  \\\"calculation\\\": {\\n    \\\"amount_expression\\\": \\\"28476342 cents / 100 = USD 284763.42\\\",\\n    \\\"late_expression\\\": \\\"2025-09-30T19:15:00 - 2025-09-30T18:00:00 = 4500 seconds = 75 minutes\\\",\\n    \\\"service\\\": \\\"data_query datetime_difference\\\",\\n    \\\"service_result_seconds\\\": 4500,\\n    \\\"start_timestamp_basis\\\": \\\"Own public cost_periods row\\\",\\n    \\\"end_timestamp_basis\\\": \\\"Shared peer report, not own public resource\\\",\\n    \\\"note\\\": \\\"The datetime service computes supplied timestamps; it does not independently retrieve or verify the event timestamp.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"policy\\\": {\\n    \\\"source_resource_id\\\": \\\"r_e8782756575fcef65a5c87b2\\\",\\n    \\\"source_file\\\": \\\"workspace/02_Cost_Accounting/oracle_supply_chain_cost_management_26b.pdf\\\",\\n    \\\"pdf_page\\\": 233,\\n    \\\"printed_page\\\": 225,\\n    \\\"section\\\": \\\"Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting\\\",\\n    \\\"rule\\\": \\\"New transactions falling in or before a Pending Close period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting and are processed after the period closes or reopens. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed. Transactions created after Pending Close are not processed, except that revenue lines, COGS recognition and manual cost adjustments continue to be processed.\\\",\\n    \\\"application\\\": \\\"The peer-reported event is a newly created component-issue INPUT event dated Sep-25, not one of the listed exceptions; POSTED therefore conflicts with that rule on the supplied period state.\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"provenance\\